<article class="env-definition" id="006T">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/006T">Definition <span data-tag="006T">6.7.1</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a topological space. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
A <em>sheaf $\mathcal{F}$ of sets on $X$</em> is a presheaf of sets which satisfies the following additional property: Given any open covering $U = \bigcup _{i \in I} U_ i$ and any collection of sections $s_ i \in \mathcal{F}(U_ i)$, $i \in I$ such that $\forall i, j\in I$ 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  s_ i|_{U_ i \cap U_ j} = s_ j|_{U_ i \cap U_ j}  \]
</div>
<p>
 there exists a unique section $s \in \mathcal{F}(U)$ such that $s_ i = s|_{U_ i}$ for all $i \in I$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
A <em>morphism of sheaves of sets</em> is simply a morphism of presheaves of sets. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
The category of sheaves of sets on $X$ is denoted $\mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (X)$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>